# Test file conventions

Match the stack already in the repo. If none exists yet:

- TypeScript / React / Spatika: Vitest + Testing Library + `jsdom` + `@testing-library/jest-dom`
- Python: `unittest` (no extra install) or `pytest` if the project already uses it

## React / Spatika

```tsx
import { render, screen } from "@testing-library/react";
import userEvent from "@testing-library/user-event";
import { describe, expect, it, vi } from "vitest";
import { SpatikaThemeProvider } from "@spatika/react";
import { SaveButton } from "./SaveButton";

describe("SaveButton", () => {
  it("calls onSave when pressed", async () => {
    const user = userEvent.setup();
    const onSave = vi.fn();
    render(
      <SpatikaThemeProvider defaultTheme="mukta" syncDocument={false}>
        <SaveButton onSave={onSave} />
      </SpatikaThemeProvider>,
    );
    await user.click(screen.getByRole("button", { name: "Save" }));
    expect(onSave).toHaveBeenCalledTimes(1);
  });
});
```

- Colocate: `SaveButton.tsx` → `SaveButton.test.tsx`
- Cover the happy path plus the important empty / disabled / error path
- Do not mock Spatika primitives unless you are testing a boundary that must not render them

## Python

```python
import unittest
from steering_check import paired_test_paths

class PairedTestPaths(unittest.TestCase):
    def test_typescript_colocation(self):
        paths = paired_test_paths("src/lib/format.ts")
        self.assertIn("src/lib/format.test.ts", paths)
```

Name tests as behavior: `test_rejects_empty_title`, not `test_1`.
